# `dfo::ltmads_blackbox_minimizer`

Minimises a black box with LT-MADS, mesh adaptive direct search with random lower-triangular poll directions.

## Signature

```cpp
dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome dfo::ltmads_blackbox_minimizer(const std::function<dfo::BlackboxEvaluation(const pluss::Series &)> &blackbox, const pluss::Series &initial, const dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig &config = {});
template <class Fn> dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome dfo::ltmads_blackbox_minimizer(Fn &&blackbox, const pluss::Series &initial, const dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig &config = {});
```

## What It Does

The same solver as [`mads_blackbox_minimizer`](mads_blackbox_minimizer.md) with the poll scheme fixed to `LtMadsRandom2N`: the directions come from a random lower-triangular integer matrix, the original MADS construction, drawn from `rng_seed`. A different seed gives a different run.

## Parameters

`Fn &&blackbox`
: A callable returning a `BlackboxEvaluation`, a `Series` of objectives or a number.

`const pluss::Series &initial`
: The starting point.

`const dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig &config`
: The settings.

## Returns

A [`BlackboxAdvancedOutcome`](BlackboxAdvancedOutcome.md).

## Errors

- A black box that returns neither objectives nor a failure flag throws on the first call.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The Rosenbrock valley.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    e.objectives = ((b - a * a).square() * 100.0 + (1.0 - a).square()).reshape({1});
    return e;
  };

  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::ltmads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0}));
  out.writeln("minimum =", o.scalarized_minimum, ", evaluations =", o.diagnostics.evaluations);
}
```

### Example 2

Seeds. The same seed repeats a run and a different one gives another.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    e.objectives = ((b - a * a).square() * 100.0 + (1.0 - a).square()).reshape({1});
    return e;
  };

  for (const std::uint64_t seed : {1, 1, 2}) {
    dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig config;
    config.rng_seed = seed;
    out.writeln("seed", seed, ": evaluations =", dfo::ltmads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0}), config).diagnostics.evaluations);
  }
}
```

### Example 3

Bounds.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    e.objectives = (x - 3.0).square().sum().reshape({1});   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)
    return e;
  };

  dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig config;
  config.lower_bounds = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  config.upper_bounds = pluss::series::make({2.0, 2.0});
  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::ltmads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({0.5, 0.5}), config);
  out.writeln("minimizer =", o.minimizer.items<double>());
}
```

